A collection of nitpicks that I picked up over time from my advisors,
coauthors, and colleagues.  I am documenting them here because my memory is
failing me of late.

Updates as of 2026: With Claude Code, many of the nitpicks here can be turned into a SKILLs file for Claude Code. This could check and fix:
1. SI unit typesetting
2. Grammatical mistakes.
3. Typos.
4. Critical, but fair minded reviewing in the style of NINES
5. Many types of reviewers:
  * Is the problem well-motivated?
  * Is the evaluation well-done?
  * Is the writing clear?
  * Is it fair to related work?
6. Checking define-before-use errors in writing.

skills/ holds the ones that exist so far. To use a skill, copy or symlink its
directory into ~/.claude/skills/ (available in every project) or into
<project>/.claude/skills/ (that project only), then ask Claude to proofread:

  ln -s "$PWD/skills/proofread-paper" ~/.claude/skills/proofread-paper

- skills/proofread-paper: pre-submission copy-editing pass over a LaTeX paper.
  Reads the rendered PDF rather than the .tex source, because source-level
  reading misses sentences that are split across a commented-out line. Covers
  most of paper_format_checklist.txt, writing_checklist.txt, and
  citation_checklist.txt, plus dangling refs, leaked review annotations, orphan
  floats, and figure numbers that point at the wrong figure.
